  clipName: RightWallLean_Loop
  author: Juno
  rigVersion: SubwayCarry-Dummy-01
  rigSignature: 415899A36E5F36473438AE1BC4FE6EC914F96F9E5C882A7651388F4C7C395EF5
  description: 'Repeat a relaxed right-wall lean with subtle breathing. Support the
    body through the outside of the right upper arm, from shoulder to elbow, against
    the wall. Open the right armpit slightly, keep the elbow low and only gently
    bent, and let the forearm and hand hang naturally downward. The left upper arm
    rests closely against the side of the torso and hangs down parallel to the tilted
    torso. Do not lift or spread it sideways. The relaxed arm points only slightly
    toward the back and stays outside the torso throughout the breathing loop. Weight
    stays over the planted right leg; the left knee is soft and the left heel is
    lifted with the toes planted. Preserve root position and foot contact throughout
    the loop. 60 fps with keys at 0, 30, 60, 90, 120. Frame 120 exactly matches frame
    0 and the adjoining Start/Exit poses. Refinement: the right leg is the nearly
    straight weight-bearing support (about 6 degrees of knee flexion) throughout
    the supported lean. Both feet keep their authored contact positions; the relaxed
    left knee and raised heel are retained.'
  sourceRig: {fileID: 1648686333044378150, guid: 9d1a15a96145a924e838aae19388632a, type: 3}
